      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14191822/assets/3bfe01c879d52b6b0cb6dbde604b506a173885ffad258cd9fa52ec298d579201.png)\n\nFind the value of $x$ in the figure above.",
      "worked_solution": "Since the exterior angles of a triangle sum to ${360}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{80}^{∘}+(x-{20}^{∘})+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 2x+{60}^{∘} & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ 2x & ={300}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={150}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
